Two directories carry their own upstream terms, because they derive from other
projects rather than from this one. The MIT grant above does not extend to them:

- `tools/findmy/` — Apache License 2.0. The Find My read began as a fork of the
  BlueBubbles helper (https://github.com/BlueBubblesApp) and keeps that
  project's license and attribution. See `tools/findmy/README.md`.

- `tools/call/blackhole.patch` — GNU General Public License v3.0. It is a diff
  against BlackHole (https://github.com/ExistentialAudio/BlackHole), which is
  GPL-3.0, so the patch inherits those terms. It patches a separate program and
  is not linked into this one. See `tools/call/README.md`.
